            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54060",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-pillow: Pillow: Denial of Service via excessive memory allocation when processing font files"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/FontFile.py FontFile.compile() assembled per-glyph images into a combined bitmap with Image.new(\"1\", (xsize, ysize)) without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), allowing a font to trigger excessive allocation during conversion or saving. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54060",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54060\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: pillow\nFixed Version: 12.3.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-54060](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54060)\nPillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/FontFile.py FontFile.compile() assembled per-glyph images into a combined bitmap with Image.new(\"1\", (xsize, ysize)) without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), allowing a font to trigger excessive allocation during conversion or saving. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54060**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|pillow|12.3.0|[CVE-2026-54060](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-54060)|\n\nPillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/FontFile.py FontFile.compile() assembled per-glyph images into a combined bitmap with Image.new(\"1\", (xsize, ysize)) without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), allowing a font to trigger excessive allocation during conversion or saving. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
