            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-55379",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-pillow: Pillow: Denial of Service via crafted BDF font file"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/BdfFontFile.py bdf_char() read the BBX width and height field from a BDF font file and passed attacker-controlled dimensions to Image.new() without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), bypassing Pillow's documented decompression bomb protection and allowing excessive memory allocation. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55379",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-55379\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: pillow\nFixed Version: 12.3.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-55379](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55379)\nPillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/BdfFontFile.py bdf_char() read the BBX width and height field from a BDF font file and passed attacker-controlled dimensions to Image.new() without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), bypassing Pillow's documented decompression bomb protection and allowing excessive memory allocation. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-55379**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|pillow|12.3.0|[CVE-2026-55379](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55379)|\n\nPillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 12.3.0, PIL/BdfFontFile.py bdf_char() read the BBX width and height field from a BDF font file and passed attacker-controlled dimensions to Image.new() without calling Image._decompression_bomb_check(), bypassing Pillow's documented decompression bomb protection and allowing excessive memory allocation. This issue is fixed in version 12.3.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H",
